162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The Enterprise Network Configuration and Security Implementation Using Cisco Packet Tracer project focuses on designing, configuring, and analyzing a secure small-scale enterprise network using Cisco Packet Tracer. The primary objective of the project is to understand the fundamentals of computer networking, wireless communication, and basic cybersecurity practices through hands-on simulation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The project involves configuring a wireless router, connecting wired and wireless client devices, assigning IP addresses using Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol \(DHCP\), and verifying network connectivity through various networking tools and commands. The simulated network enables communication between devices while demonstrating how routers, switches, IP addressing, and wireless technologies work together to provide reliable and secure network connectivity.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (In addition to network configuration, the project emphasizes essential cybersecurity concepts such as secure wireless network configuration, authentication, firewall awareness, traffic monitoring, and protection against common network threats. Connectivity testing and troubleshooting techniques are performed to ensure proper communication between network devices and to identify potential configuration issues.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (This project provides practical exposure to enterprise networking concepts, including IP addressing, routing, switching, packet forwarding, and wireless security. By using Cisco Packet Tracer, a realistic network environment is created where theoretical networking concepts can be implemented and analyzed without requiring physical networking equipment. The project enhances practical skills in network design, configuration, troubleshooting, and security, providing a strong foundation for further studies and careers in networking and cybersecurity.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
