234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (As part of the internship, a project titled "Enterprise Network Configuration and Security Implementation Using Cisco Packet Tracer" was carried out to simulate and configure a secure small-scale enterprise network. The objective of the project was to gain practical knowledge of network design, device configuration, wireless communication, IP addressing, and basic cybersecurity concepts using Cisco Packet Tracer.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The project began by designing a network topology consisting of a cable modem, home wireless router, office desktop computer, bedroom desktop computer, laptop, television, and an external server connected through the Internet. Both wired and wireless connections were established to simulate a real-world home/office network environment.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The wireless router was configured with appropriate network parameters, including the SSID, wireless security settings, and DHCP service. The DHCP server was enabled to automatically assign IPv4 addresses, subnet masks, default gateway addresses, and DNS server information to all client devices, eliminating the need for manual IP configuration.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The office desktop computer was connected to the router using an Ethernet cable and successfully obtained its IP configuration through DHCP. The laptop was configured to connect securely to the wireless network using the configured wireless profile and authentication settings. Network connectivity between all connected devices was verified after successful association with the wireless access point.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (After completing the network configuration, communication between devices and external resources was tested. The office PC successfully accessed the wireless router's web-based management interface, confirming proper network configuration and router accessibility. The bedroom PC successfully accessed the hosted web server through the simulated Internet, demonstrating end-to-end connectivity, proper DNS resolution, and successful packet forwarding across the network.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
